; geekamp and the classic label are 32-bit DLLs (present.txt "pe32": run-plan.ps1 writes
; a minimal PE32 header), old64 is a 64-bit one. Label.dll is not installed, so label-1.99
; falls back to the original, which is 32-bit too. Nothing is mapped: no Core item.
LoadModule $LiteStepDir$old64.dll
*NetLoadModule geekamp-1.9.7
*NetLoadModule label-1.99
